WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.039
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Saturday, November twenty first.

2
00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:12.630
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.145
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:29.661
Today: a strong earthquake in central Peru, two tanker attacks near the Strait of Hormuz, Russian missiles and a drone in Polish airspace, new U.S. sanctions on Iran's oil trade, and planned protests across France this weekend.

5
00:00:29.661 --> 00:00:30.598
We start in Peru.

6
00:00:30.598 --> 00:00:31.460
The U.S.

7
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:41.925
Geological Survey reported a magnitude six point seven earthquake in the Junín region of central Peru on Friday evening, at a depth of more than one hundred kilometers.

8
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:56.783
Peru's civil defense institute, INDECI, reports damage to homes, a hospital in Pichanaqui, churches and roads across Junín, Pasco, Huánuco and Lima, along with power outages, and rockfalls restricting traffic on routes including the Lima to Huancayo highway.

9
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:57.761
In Lima, rocks fell onto the Costa Verde coastal road.

10
00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:06.144
State broadcaster TV Peru reports the head of INDECI said no injuries had been reported.

11
00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:08.095
Turning to the Strait of Hormuz.

12
00:01:08.095 --> 00:01:12.452
Reuters reports two tanker attack incidents near Khasab, Oman, today, according to the U.K.

13
00:01:12.452 --> 00:01:15.693
Maritime Trade Operations center.

14
00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:23.108
Separately, the Institute for the Study of War assesses Iran will likely attempt to run the U.S. naval blockade in the coming days.

15
00:01:23.108 --> 00:01:24.670
Next, Poland.

16
00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:36.138
Reuters reports three Russian objects, believed to be two missiles and a drone, violated Polish airspace overnight into Friday, and Poland's defense minister called it a provocation by Moscow.

17
00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:45.513
The Institute for the Study of War assesses the Kremlin conducted the violations intentionally, to coincide with an ongoing Coalition of the Willing military exercise.

18
00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:55.306
In Ukraine, an update on Friday's overnight attack: Radio Free Europe Radio Liberty reports at least nine people were killed and twenty eight injured across the country.

19
00:01:55.306 --> 00:01:56.570
On sanctions.

20
00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.904
The Treasury Department says it is targeting key oil trustees the Iranian regime relies on to sell oil abroad, as part of what it calls Operation Economic Outcast.

21
00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:11.112
The State Department spokesperson said four Iranian regime insiders were sanctioned.

22
00:02:11.112 --> 00:02:16.666
Reuters also reports Treasury is pressing Singapore and Malaysia on Iran sanctions compliance.

23
00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:25.465
And in France, the State Department says protests and rallies continue across the country, with multiple groups planning demonstrations for today and tomorrow.

24
00:02:25.465 --> 00:02:33.227
It notes protests can occur outside planned routes, and some past demonstrations were violent and involved property destruction and looting.

25
00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:36.589
Now a few quick notes by region.

26
00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:41.236
In the Middle East, Smartraveller updated its Saudi Arabia advice, still at do not travel.

27
00:02:41.236 --> 00:02:54.442
It says the Houthis have targeted or threatened energy facilities, offices, airports and Red Sea ports, including in Riyadh and Dammam, and that Riyadh's King Abdullah Financial District has also been targeted.

28
00:02:54.442 --> 00:02:56.149
In Africa, an update on Ethiopia.

29
00:02:56.149 --> 00:03:05.847
Critical Threats says the Ethiopian military reportedly resumed fighting with Eritrean and Tigray People's Liberation Front forces around the Eritrean border town of Badme.

30
00:03:05.847 --> 00:03:20.104
In Sudan, ACLED and Critical Threats say the Sudanese Armed Forces have made significant westward advances in central Sudan, and ACLED says the army's advances toward Al Nuhud in West Kordofan are putting pressure on R S F positions.

31
00:03:20.104 --> 00:03:33.517
In Asia, Thai P B S World reports suspected insurgents carried out coordinated early morning attacks in Narathiwat province in Thailand's deep south, setting off explosions, burning tires and targeting surveillance cameras.

32
00:03:33.517 --> 00:03:34.017
And the U.S.

33
00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:40.875
Geological Survey reported a magnitude six point eight earthquake in the Banda Sea, northeast of Timor Leste.

34
00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:49.514
In Central Asia, Travel Canada says the Bedel border crossing between Kyrgyzstan and China is closed, and that crossings may close without notice.

35
00:03:49.514 --> 00:03:58.602
In Europe, the State Department says a public transport strike with a union protest is scheduled in Belgium for Monday, November twenty third.

36
00:03:58.602 --> 00:04:00.094
In the Americas, the U.K.

37
00:04:00.094 --> 00:04:13.323
Foreign Office says Ecuador has extended its state of emergency for another thirty days in eight provinces, including Guayas, Pichincha and Esmeraldas, with greater police and military presence on the streets.

38
00:04:13.323 --> 00:04:30.627
On aviation security, Times Now reports the F B I, the Department of Homeland Security and the T S A warned U.S. airlines, cargo carriers and airports about al Qaeda messages calling for attacks on aircraft, including hijackings like September's attempted hijacking of a Tel Aviv bound Flydubai flight.

39
00:04:30.627 --> 00:04:39.249
And on cyber threats, The Record reports hackers exploited a software supplier's vulnerability to breach more than forty Irish credit unions.

40
00:04:39.249 --> 00:04:41.730
Reuters, citing NBC News, reports hackers breached the U.S.

41
00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.078
Department of Agriculture.

42
00:04:45.078 --> 00:04:46.508
That's today's brief.

43
00:04:46.508 --> 00:04:54.902
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

44
00:04:54.902 --> 00:05:03.230
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

45
00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.456
This brief is digitally narrated.

46
00:05:05.456 --> 00:05:06.443
Questions?

47
00:05:06.443 --> 00:05:09.954
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

48
00:05:09.954 --> 00:05:12.192
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
